# Player progress knob: draw through the keyed helper.
name: 0118-progress-knob-keyed
kind: module
module: 27
region: code
address: 0x307f79a
gate: build refuses unless the stock bytes at the target equal
  `expect`; the finished image must also pass the grown
  build validator. Pairs with the keyed knob art (resources 220
  and 386) in patches/antialias/screens-glyphs.json.
expect: e3f7d6fe
replace: e4f735f9
rationale: The progress segment of module 27's player Display fills
  (40, 254)..(201, 268) with the ground, draws the bar columns, then
  draws the knob (resource 220, light 386) with DrawImageAt
  (0x0306354A), which is opaque. The stock knob's corners are baked
  dark, so over a theater ground taken from cover art the knob sat in
  a dark square. This BL now targets the keyed helper 0x03063A08,
  which takes the same (id, x, y) and skips 0xF800, and the knob art
  is a keyed disc with an antialiased edge. The bar area is refilled
  with the ground before every knob draw, so a moving knob leaves no
  trace. It is the only draw of 220/386 in the firmware (scan of
  every module for a `movs r0, #0xdc` / `#0x182` before a BL).
